course: dictionary
lesson: 2734
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and direction is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues. «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars, because light from very distant stars has not had time to reach us, and so in most directions our sight runs out into darkness.» Here direction means a way something points, because sight runs out in every way we look.
explain: «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» Here direction means the way something goes. Test it: swap in the word way. «Sound spreads out in every way» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: «The friends, listening from under a leaf, are worried: even Jaguar cannot forget such clear directions.» Here directions means instructions that tell you how to get somewhere. The clues are clear and forget: you can forget steps, but not clear steps you need to follow.
explain: Direction can also mean leading or guiding people, like a film director does. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Direction means the way something goes, faces or points, like north, left, up or forwards.
fact: Directions (plural) are instructions that tell you how to get somewhere or how to do something.
fact: Direction can also mean leading or guiding people, like a film director does.
fact: «In the direction of» means towards something, and «opposite direction» means the other way round.
fact: «Each letter has a correct starting point and direction; most small letters start at the top.»
exercise: «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance.» What does direction mean here? | A film director | *The way the sound goes | Instructions for getting home | A type of weather
exercise: «Even Jaguar cannot forget such clear directions.» What are the directions here? | The points of a compass on a map only | *Instructions that tell you how to get somewhere | Sounds that spread far | A way of leading a film
exercise: «Follow the directions on the packet.» What are the directions? | Lines that point up to the sky | Sounds that get weaker with distance | *Instructions that tell you what to do | People who lead a film
test: «The light went in the opposite direction.» What does direction mean here? | *The way something points or goes | Instructions for a journey | A loud noise | A kind of film
test: A film director does what to the actors? | Sells the tickets | *Leads and guides them | Sings the loudest | Sweeps the floor
exam: Read «The friends, listening from under a leaf, are worried: even Jaguar cannot forget such clear directions.» Which meaning of direction fits best, and why? | Sound going far | Leading a film | The way the leaf faces | *Instructions to get somewhere, because clear and forget show steps to remember
